; Start AmiGTA with the stack it needs.
;
; RUN THIS FROM THE GAME'S OWN DRAWER:
;
;     cd DH1:Games/AmiGTA
;     execute run
;
; There is nothing to assign. The game finds its data through PROGDIR:, the
; drawer the executable itself was loaded from, so it works wherever you put
; it. Up to v0.0.1 every path was hard-coded to Work: and the README had to
; tell you to assign Work: to the game drawer - that was a bug with a
; workaround printed next to it, and people quite reasonably asked what the
; work directory was supposed to be.
;
; Stack: libnix gives a CLI process 4 KB by default. That is nowhere near
; enough for a game that recurses through map and sprite loading; the OpenTTD
; and OpenXcom ports both needed 1 MB for the same reason. The .info files
; carry the same number for a Workbench double-click.
;
; There is one binary. Up to v0.0.3 there were three - gta-aga, gta-rtg240
; and gta-rtg480 - which differed only in the screen size compiled into them.
; The size and the display path are settings now: run `gtaprefs` (or edit
; gta.prefs by hand; the words are in it) and start the same game either way.
;
; This file is the version-controlled template. tools/bin/deploy.sh copies it
; to the emulator's shared folder (adding a CD for the unattended test rig)
; and tools/bin/package.sh ships it as-is; edit it here, not there.
Stack 1000000
AmiGTA >gta.log
